  $$Carolina Rojas Villalobos is a writer and editor who has spent ten years turning complex governance research into reports that ministers and citizens read. Much of her work sits inside public procurement and anti-corruption programmes: she co-authored the procurement audit reports of a regional transparency programme in Guatemala and Honduras, analysed red flags in contract data alongside the audit teams, and wrote the guidance that community committees use for citizen engagement in monitoring public works. She has also drafted trade and investment climate studies for regional economic bodies. Carolina works in Spanish, English and Portuguese and is often brought in at the analysis stage, not only for the final edit. She also writes on regional trade facilitation and translates reports between Spanish and English.$$,
