  $$https://randomuser.me/api/portraits/women/96.jpg$$,
  $$https://picsum.photos/seed/demo-lucia-barrios-cifuentes/800/200$$,
  $$Lucía Barrios Cifuentes has worked on public procurement reform and anti-corruption in Central America for nineteen years. She served as deputy director of Guatemala's procurement regulator, where she oversaw rules for the Guatecompras portal, and later advised procurement authorities in Honduras and El Salvador on adopting the Open Contracting Data Standard. As a consultant she has led integrity assessments of the procurement cycle, designed red-flag indicators for emergency procurement, and evaluated social audit programmes in which community committees monitor public works. She combines legal and institutional analysis with policy analysis that ministries can act on, and is an experienced facilitator of multi-stakeholder dialogue between government, auditors, bidders and civil-society organizations. She also supports civil society organisations and indigenous women's participation in local oversight.$$,
