  $$https://picsum.photos/seed/demo-rania-haddad/800/200$$,
  $$Rania Haddad has researched refugee response and social cohesion in Lebanon, Jordan and Syria for sixteen years. She designs mixed-methods studies of tension between refugee and host communities, combining household surveys, focus groups and conflict analysis, and turns them into conflict-sensitive programme recommendations. She has led social cohesion assessments in Tripoli, Akkar and the Bekaa for UN agencies and NGO consortia, evaluated the tension-monitoring system of the Lebanon Crisis Response Plan, and advised municipalities on dialogue mechanisms around services and jobs. Rania's qualitative research is known for reaching people who rarely speak to surveys: young men in informal work, women running home-based businesses, and landlords. She teaches a course on conflict-sensitive research methods at a university in Beirut. She also researches media narratives about refugees and trains municipal staff in conflict sensitivity.$$,
