  $$Nguyễn Thu Hà is an agribusiness specialist who has worked with smallholder farmers and agri-SMEs across Vietnam, the Philippines and Indonesia for twelve years. Her work sits where value chains meet finance: she has run market research on the credit needs of coffee and rice cooperatives, built financial modeling tools that agricultural lenders use to price seasonal loans, and helped seaweed processors design supplier finance for the farmers who sell to them. She has worked on financial inclusion projects for IFAD and the World Bank and with impact investors entering Southeast Asian agriculture. Hà is a practical facilitator who brings farmers, lenders and buyers into the same room to agree on how credit and repayment should follow the harvest. She also works with seaweed and shrimp farmers on climate adaptation and with women's farmer groups.$$,
